{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5521) to implement `cmd/basenc/main.go` - the basenc utility for the go-unix-utils project. This utility supports multiple encoding algorithms (--base64, --base64url, --base32, --base32hex, --base16, --z85) with configurable line wrapping. The task covers srd081-basenc requirements R1.1-R1.4 (encoding scheme selection and encoding execution), plus wrapping (R2.4) and stdin/file input handling (R3.2). The title says \"R1.1-R1.4\" but the acceptance criteria explicitly require all six encoding modes and proper error handling for missing/multiple flags.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - pkg/encutil provides `EncoderConfig`, `Encode()`, and `OpenInput()` for shared encoding logic\n   - pkg/sys provides `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - Go's `encoding/base64`, `encoding/base32`, `encoding/hex` stdlib packages for encoding implementations\n   - Z85 encoding (ZeroMQ variant) - needs custom implementation as Go stdlib doesn't provide it\n   - RFC 4648 Base64, Base64URL, Base32, Base32hex encodings\n   - Default wrap column is 76; -w 0 disables wrapping\n   - Exactly one encoding flag must be specified (D4)\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Copyright header required on all files\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd081-basenc.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for basenc utility with R1 (encoding schemes: base64, base64url, base32, base32hex), R2 (additional encodings: base16, z85, decode flag, wrap), R3 (input handling, error cases, SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: no Base2 encoding, no custom alphabets\n     - Key requirements for this task: R1.1-R1.4 encoding scheme flags, R2.1 base16, R2.2 z85, R2.4 wrap, R3.2 stdin/file, R3.3 error exit, R3.4 SIGPIPE\n   \n   - `pkg/encutil/encode.go` (provided in context)\n     - Provides `EncoderConfig{Encode func([]byte) string, WrapCol int}` and `Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error`\n     - `writeWrapped()` handles line wrapping internally\n     ```go\n     type EncoderConfig struct {\n         Encode  func([]byte) string\n         WrapCol int\n     }\n     func Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` (provided in context)\n     - Provides `OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)` - returns os.Stdin for \"\" or \"-\"\n     - Provides `DecoderConfig` and `Decode()` for decode mode (not needed for this task's scope)\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (provided in context)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - installs SIGPIPE handler for graceful exit 0\n\n   - `cmd/basenc/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Main implementation file for the basenc utility\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only read the SRD before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand full requirements before implementation\n   - Need to handle Z85 encoding which is not in Go's stdlib - will need a custom Z85 encoder\n   - The task says R1.1-R1.4 but AC3 requires all six encoding modes, so all must be implemented\n   - Need to determine how to parse flags - likely use flag package directly (no cobra for cmd/ utilities based on existing patterns)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task prompt with full project context, SRDs, source code, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, constraints, and acceptance criteria for implementing cmd/basenc encoding mode.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a 